Use `lib.optionals` (not `lib.optional`) for list-valued buildInputs deps.

`mk-poetry-dep.nix` built each dependency's `buildInputs` with `lib.optional`,
which wraps its argument in a singleton list. Both arguments here are already
lists — `(getManyLinuxDeps …).pkg` and `buildSystemPkgs` — so the result was a
nested list (`[ [ … ] ]`).

Nixpkgs 26.05 deprecates nested lists in dependency attributes
(pkgs/stdenv/generic/make-derivation.nix), emitting one
"uses a nested list in attribute 'buildInputs'" warning per locked package.
This spams the eval log of every downstream consumer (e.g. kubeseal-auto).

`lib.optionals` concatenates the list instead of wrapping it — the correct
combinator — which silences the warnings.

Upstream poetry2nix is dormant since April 2025; patch locally until fixed
(nix-community/poetry2nix).

--- a/mk-poetry-dep.nix
+++ b/mk-poetry-dep.nix
@@ -140,8 +140,8 @@
         hooks.pipBuildHook
       ];

-      buildInputs = lib.optional isLocked (getManyLinuxDeps fileInfo.name).pkg
-        ++ lib.optional isDirectory buildSystemPkgs;
+      buildInputs = lib.optionals isLocked (getManyLinuxDeps fileInfo.name).pkg
+        ++ lib.optionals isDirectory buildSystemPkgs;

       propagatedBuildInputs =
         let
